* Minimoog Model D oscillator board No. 1, "old" board (serial numbers below 10175):
* what oscillators 2 and 3 have that oscillator 1 has not. Their cores, converters and
* shapers are mm_vco (board1-vco.lib) under their own designators.
*
* Source drawing: service manual Figure 9-3 (S-F93), the front panel's controls from
* Figure 9-17 (S-F917); docs/circuit/board1.md, "Oscillators 2 and 3".

* --- oscillator 2's FREQUENCY network --------------------------------------------------
* The front panel's OSCILLATOR-2 FREQUENCY (R4 5K linear, +10 V to R35 5.1K to GND) comes
* in on 12A through R95 220K to IC4's + input, which R87 91K pulls toward -10 V and R94
* 1K (mm_vco's R10) holds near the -5 V line: millivolts of offset, about 17 semitones over
* the pot's travel ("+- a musical fifth").
*   freq  12A, the pot's wiper (+5.05..+10 V)
*   pos   IC4 pin 3 (mm_vco's pos)
.subckt mm_osc2freq freq pos vn
r95   freq pos 220k                 ; R95 220K
r87   pos vn 91k                    ; R87 91K
.ends mm_osc2freq

* --- oscillator 3's control stage IC8 ------------------------------------------------------
* OSCILLATOR-3 FREQUENCY (R5 5K linear, +10 V to R41 5.1K to GND) drives IC8 through R181
* 51K (9A) and, with OSC. 3 CONTROL off, through R180 15K too (10A, joined by the switch):
* IC8 inverts it about its + input (R150 1K from +10 V over R155 3.01K to GND: 7.51 V, the
* pot's centre), with R170 15K feedback and R162 3.01K from +10 V, so its output sits at
* -5.0 V (oscillator 3's summing junction) with the pot centred and R143 51.1K carries its
* change into oscillator 3's summing junction: about +- a fifth with the switch on, about
* +-3 octaves with it off. The service manual's text for this board (2.18) says only that
* SW2 "interrupts the keyboard, modulation, external, and pitchbend voltage on oscillator
* three and also increases the range" of its control; the figures are the later board's
* (2.3: "+- a musical fifth", "+- 3 octaves"), and 5.36 checks this board's wide range (LO,
* the pot at minimum: a click every 2 to 5 s).
*   tune  9A, the pot's wiper             ctl  10A (open, or the wiper when the switch is off)
*   sum   oscillator 3's summing junction (IC6 pin 2, 15A)
.subckt mm_osc3ctl tune ctl sum vp vn
r181  tune inv 51k                  ; R181 51K (56K before modification 8.2)
r180  ctl inv 15k                   ; R180 15K
r162  vp inv 3.01k                  ; R162 3.01K 1% (modification 8.2, kit 94-001; the drawing: 3K)
r170  out inv 15k                   ; R170 15K 1%
r150  vp pos8 1k                    ; R150 1K
r155  pos8 0 3.01k                  ; R155 3.01K 1%
xic8  pos8 inv vp vn out ua741      ; IC8 741
r143  out sum 51.1k                 ; R143 51.1K 1%
.ends mm_osc3ctl

* --- oscillator 3's reverse sawtooth: Q37 -------------------------------------------------
* A shunt-feedback inverter on oscillator 3's sawtooth output (13B, through R171 33K): R175
* 68K from collector to base, R182 390K to -10 V, emitter at GND; its collector (R165 2.2K
* from +10 V through R164 330, decoupled by C10 2.2 uF) level-shifted through R172 7.5K
* against R176 18K to -10 V to the output 7B ("+1.7 to -1.7 V loaded"). The drawing labels
* the 7.5K "R175"; Table 7-5 has R172 7.5K and R175 68K.
*   saw   13B, oscillator 3's sawtooth     rev  7B, the reverse sawtooth
.subckt mm_revsaw saw rev vp vn
r164  vp na 330                     ; R164 330
c10   na 0 2.2u                     ; C10 2.2 uF / 50 V
r165  na c37 2.2k                   ; R165 2.2K
r175  c37 b37 68k                   ; R175 68K
r171  saw b37 33k                   ; R171 33K
r182  b37 vn 390k                   ; R182 390K
q37   c37 b37 0 Q2N3392             ; Q37 2N3392
r172  c37 rev 7.5k                  ; R172 7.5K
r176  rev vn 18k                    ; R176 18K
.ends mm_revsaw
